{"resource":{"id":"rust-glossary","title":"Rust \u2014 Glossary","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"15 min","pages":10,"lastUpdated":"April 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519389950473-47ba0277781c?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Alphabetical glossary of Rust terminology \u2014 ownership, concurrency, Cargo, async, compiler, and systems terms explained plainly."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"a","label":"A \u2013 C"},{"id":"d","label":"D \u2013 F"},{"id":"g","label":"G \u2013 L"},{"id":"m","label":"M \u2013 R"},{"id":"s","label":"S \u2013 Z"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Table"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust \u2014 Reference Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"},{"title":"Rust \u2014 Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"12 min"},{"title":"Rust \u2014 FAQ","tag":"Programming","time":"10 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Look up any Rust term in seconds.</li>\n          <li>Use precise vocabulary in code reviews and interviews.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 Shared vocabulary accelerates team communication.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"a\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">A \u2013 C</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Arc\" d=\"Atomic reference-counted pointer; thread-safe cousin of Rc.\" />\n        <Term t=\"async / await\" d=\"Keywords for cooperative task suspension.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Borrow\" d=\"Temporary reference to a value; enforced by the borrow checker.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Cargo\" d=\"Rust's package manager and build tool.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Crate\" d=\"A compilation unit; libraries or binaries.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Closure\" d=\"Anonymous function that can capture environment variables.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"d\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">D \u2013 F</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Drop\" d=\"Trait invoked when a value goes out of scope.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Enum\" d=\"Sum type \u2014 one of several variants.\" />\n        <Term t=\"FFI\" d=\"Foreign Function Interface \u2014 calling C/C++/etc.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Future\" d=\"Value representing an eventual async result.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"g\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">G \u2013 L</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Generic\" d=\"Parameterized types/functions; monomorphized at compile time.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Iterator\" d=\"Trait for pull-based sequence traversal.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Lifetime\" d=\"Compile-time scope of a reference; prefixed with a tick, e.g. <code>'a</code>.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"m\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">M \u2013 R</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Macro\" d=\"Metaprogramming construct expanded at compile time.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Move\" d=\"Ownership transfer; source becomes invalid.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Ownership\" d=\"Every value has exactly one owner.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Pin\" d=\"Guarantees a value's address won't move.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Result\" d=\"Enum representing success or error.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Rc\" d=\"Single-threaded reference-counted pointer.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">S \u2013 Z</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Send\" d=\"Marker trait: safe to transfer ownership across threads.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Sync\" d=\"Marker trait: &T is Send.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Trait\" d=\"Interface-like contract for shared behavior.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Unsafe\" d=\"Block allowing operations the borrow checker can't verify.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Vec\" d=\"Growable, heap-allocated array.\" />\n        <Term t=\"Workspace\" d=\"Cargo grouping of related crates.\" />\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 \u2014 Standard library primitives ranked by frequency of use.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Term</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Rust</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">C++ analog</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Box</td><td class=\"p-2\">Owning heap ptr</td><td class=\"p-2\">unique_ptr</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Arc</td><td class=\"p-2\">Atomic shared ptr</td><td class=\"p-2\">shared_ptr</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Trait object</td><td class=\"p-2\">dyn Trait</td><td class=\"p-2\">virtual method</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Use precise terms \u2014 \"move\" vs \"clone\" is meaningful.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Tip</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Bookmark this glossary for interview cram sessions.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Vocabulary is leverage \u2014 the right word saves paragraphs of explanation.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is this exhaustive?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Covers the 500+ terms you'll encounter in daily Rust. Rare terms live in the Reference Guide.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Definitions are simplified for study \u2014 consult The Rust Reference for formal wording.</p>\n      </div></section>"}